# pixi environments
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml

# pixi build/publish output -- `pixi build` writes the built package
# directly into the current directory by default
*.conda

# generated test artifacts
tests/_test_*.bmp
tests/_test_*.png

# `pixi run example`'s own scratch output -- extract_docstring_
# examples.mojo writes one real, runnable .mojo file per `Example:`
# docstring section here, then scripts/run_parallel.sh compiles and
# runs every one (see pixi.toml's own `example` task). Not committed --
# regenerated fresh from dataviz_mojo/*.mojo's own docstrings each run.
.build/

# modo doc-generator binary (scripts/install-modo.sh) and its
# `mojo doc` JSON input -- regenerated by `pixi run docs`, not
# committed.
.tools/
docs/src/*.json

# docs/src/examples/ is entirely generated -- the .md pages by
# scripts/gen_example_docs.mojo and the .svg/.png/.bmp images
# themselves, both sourced from dataviz_mojo/*.mojo's own `Example:`
# docstring sections (see that script's own docstring, and pixi.toml's
# `example`/`docs-build` tasks). Only docs/src/_index.md, the landing
# page, is real hand-written source. Modo's own generated Hugo content
# and Hugo's own built static site are generated too, from docs/src/ --
# none of this is committed; all of it is deployed straight to GitHub
# Pages by .github/workflows/docs.yml's own Actions-based deploy,
# regenerated fresh on every run. docs/site/'s own Hugo *project* files
# (hugo.yaml, go.mod/go.sum) ARE committed -- those are real source,
# not output.
docs/src/examples/
docs/site/content/
docs/site/public/
docs/site/*.lock
